The Dreamer is pretty straight forward. &nbsp; Don&#39;t hit the child, defeat projections, and win. &nbsp;Wager Master is Gimmicky because the rules constantly change and that&#39;s not what happens in this fight.&nbsp;

[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

What I would recommend is taking your time before flipping the Dreamer. &nbsp;She hits everyone and plays a lot of cards. &nbsp;Make sure you get yourself setup with a buffer of Ongoings so you still have things like Sentinel Tactics and Buffer Overflow in play once flipped. &nbsp;

[/quote]

&nbsp;

...Except that if you do that, all of the heroes have been pounded into nigh-hamburger (10 HP or so), and she gets +1 damage and plays 3 cards per round. &nbsp;When HP are that low, a single Night Terrors together with an AOE projection will wipe all of your heroes in one shot. &nbsp;I know; it happened to me. &nbsp;Several times.

[quote="Manix312"]

you just gotta think outside the box on this one. there&#39;s a reason you have a bunch of heroes with irreducible damage, tucking effects (no executions), destroy at x or less hp effects, etc.yes, you aren&#39;t using most of the heroes in the standard fashion but that&#39;s okay. when i realized the trick to this is to have chrono-ranger and ra play utility it seemed fine.&nbsp;

[/quote]

&nbsp;

What good does &quot;No Executions&quot; do? &nbsp;Dreamer doesn&#39;t pull projections out of her trash (like Dawn/Voss/Chairman), nor does having projections in the trash trigger any effects (like Chairman/Dawn). &nbsp;The only use I&#39;ve found for it is to give Chrono multiple hits on Danny Boy, or more damage via Masada. &nbsp;(As many times as everybody gets hit, Hunter and Hunted just seemed like a recipe for Jim&#39;s early death.)

[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

Did you try hitting the Dreamer by Idealist as a Matchstickman suggested as well? &nbsp; Between that and not quickly forcing a flip I managed to get through this finally. &nbsp;

[/quote]

You mean on her flipped side? &nbsp; Usually by the time she flips, my heroes are so beat up that the initial 3-card onslaught with +1 damage kills them. &nbsp;I think in only 2 games have I managed to last more than a round after she&#39;s flipped. &nbsp;Reducing Dreamer&#39;s damage doesn&#39;t help so much when you have an (ex:) Dark Hero-buffed Macabre Spectre doing 4 AOE (2 +1 Dreamer +1 Dark Hero) the second it comes out. &nbsp;
